'' A declaration and its definition are ONE procedure even when only the declaration
'' says 'overload'. Collect pairs them by ARITY, because it runs before any type is
'' resolved, so a same-arity overload set left the definition to declare a symbol of
'' its own: the set then held the procedure twice, the two cost identically, and the
'' call resolved to NOTHING -- an untyped call whose consumer declined, with no
'' diagnostic. Measured: fbc mangles the definition '_Z2PRi' either way.
''
'' The string family needed an ORDER for the same reason. Every string-to-string
'' conversion cost the same, so any two string overloads tied. Measured pairwise
'' against fbc: a ZSTRING source prefers 'string', a STRING source prefers 'zstring',
'' and neither order is the other's mirror.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/overload-split.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/overload-split.out
